{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Take heed to yourself, lest you forget HaShem, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage.</b> Scripture gives warning that when abundance and tranquility increase, one should recall the days of his lowliness and affliction — that he was a slave in Egypt and had there no cities and houses as he does now — and that he not forget HaShem, who brought him out from that great bondage into this great goodness; rather, he should remember His kindnesses always and fear Him and serve before Him as a slave before his master. This is what Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Ecclesiastes 7): ״ביום טובה היה בטוב וביום רעה ראה״ — the measure of the verse is: on the day of good, look upon the day of evil; that is, while you yet have an abundance of goodness, gaze upon the day of evil that you have already experienced, and then you will find and remember the advantage you have today over the time that has passed, and give thanks to the Holy One, blessed be He, for this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:02.811981525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}